steps.prompt:
STAGE 2 — Feature Requirements.

Run id: {{run_id}}. Load the skill 'spec-driven-development' context mentally; your job here is ONLY requirements, not the spec.

Inputs:
- feature_description: {{feature_description}}
- spec_file (optional): {{spec_file}}
- docs_refs (optional): {{docs_refs}}
- acceptance_criteria (optional): {{acceptance_criteria}}
- constraints (optional): {{constraints}}

If spec_file is a non-empty path, read it. If feature_description references a GitHub issue and `gh` is available, you MAY read the issue read-only. Otherwise use the inline text. Read AGENTS.md and .kiro/steering/* for repo conventions and the existing app under {{app_dir}} to ground scope.

Produce {{docs_dir}}/requirements.md with: source, numbered REQ-<n> requirements, per-requirement acceptance criteria where derivable, clearly-labelled assumptions, and an explicit list of ambiguities/contradictions/open questions. NEVER invent business rules — unknowns go to open questions.

Record REQUIREMENTS_RETRIEVED via {{target_repo}}/tools/audit/record_event.py (--artifact {{docs_dir}}/requirements.md). Signal send_message success.
